{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014pkyMFHXqA41obp1wKeXGM","type":"tool_result","content":"58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## How amounts are stored\n61\t\n62\tWhenever you add an expense, tally converts the amount into US dollars using the\n63\tconversion table in `tally/rates.py` and stores that dollar figure. The original\n64\tamount and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total\n65\tyou ever see is computed in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a\n66\tmonth mixes several currencies.\n67\t\n68\t## A note on scope\n69\t\n70\tThis is a personal tool, not an accounting package. It does not do tax categories,\n71\treceipts, shared budgets, or anything clever with recurring expenses. If you need\n72\tthose, you have outgrown tally. If you just want to know whether you spent too much\n73\ton takeout last month, you are in the right place.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ef322a3-6143-4a71-afec-32329f72e06e","uuid":"55150d20-02ca-4fb6-ad06-876ce303527b","timestamp":"2026-07-05T20:46:26.281Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sk/.cache/speech-acts-worktrees/rep3/t24-B/README.md","content":"```\n\n## How amounts are stored\n\nWhenever you add an expense, tally converts the amount into US dollars using the\nconversion table in `tally/rates.py` and stores that dollar figure. The original\namount and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total\nyou ever see is computed in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a\nmonth mixes several currencies.\n\n## A note on scope\n\nThis is a personal tool, not an accounting package. It does not do tax categories,\nreceipts, shared budgets, or anything clever with recurring expenses. If you need\nthose, you have outgrown tally. If you just want to know whether you spent too much\non takeout last month, you are in the right place.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":58,"totalLines":74}}}
